#!RuleTest
#test PMDA-AD0352 expect=violation domain=ADLBC
#note "ZERO data rows. Firing shape is DECLARED, not populated: A1IND is a column while A1LO/A1HI/A1LOC/A1HIC are not; presence is a property of the declared schema. Expander reads aPrimary.getMetaData(), which carries the declared columns of a zero-row table, so {y=1} is still seeded; the concrete Check is 100% dataset-constant, BroadcastFold decides it against the original context before the 0-row synthetic table is built, and datasetBroadcastResult emits exactly ONE violation at internal row 0 = reported row 1. Pin row=1 and NO value pin. Precedents: pmda/PMDA-AD0170, pmda/PMDA-AD0246, pmda/PMDA-AD0499 invalid_empty_dataset fixtures. If this escalates the cause is the wildcard x 0-row interaction, not the rule - re-pin THIS fixture only."
#library standard=adamig version=1-3
#expectViolationCount 1
#expectViolationAt row=1
dataset ADLBC structure=BDS
col STUDYID type=Char
col USUBJID type=Char
col PARAMCD type=Char
col A1IND   type=Char
---
